00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.470 align:start position:0%
 
we continue our coverage of the uvalde  texas the latest unspeakable act of gun  violence in this country an 18 year old  male walked into robb elementary school  yesterday he had an  ar-15 rifle  so you heard he went classroom to  classroom opening fire and everyone in  his way at least 19 children  little children and two teachers were  killed they were just two days away from  summer vacation i can't stop thinking  about that the massacre reminds us of  this horrific shooting that killed 26  people at sandy hook elementary school  in newtown connecticut that was nearly  10 years ago now it was a crime at the  time that shook us all to the core  scott pelley anchor of the cbs evening  news said this on the day of that  shooting  we have been through this too many times  those are the words of president obama  and the thoughts of all of us after  another mass shooting in america  it is a crime more horrific than many  could have imagined in a place that no  one would have expected here in the  idyllic new england community of newtown  connecticut today a gunman opened fire  on school children in a kindergarten  classroom  earlier today a number of our citizens  beautiful children  had their life taken away from them six  seven st hook school callers indicating  she thinks there's someone shooting in  the building i saw some of the bullets  going past the hall that i was right  next to  i just heard the principal was shot and  killed  i heard  i heard some kids were  shot i missed a teacher mrs hammons was  shot who would have ever thought in  elementary school where the children  as a country we have been through this  too many times  i know there's not a parent in america  who doesn't feel the same overwhelming  grief that i do all these parents were  waiting for their children to come out  they thought that they were  you know still alive  there's 20 parents that were just told  that their children are dead  [Music]  it was awful  it was ten years ago connecticut senator  chris murphy was a congressman  representing the families of sandy hook  elementary school  since then the democrat has worked in  congress to try and pass tougher gun  laws and senator murphy joins us now  senator i look at those images and i'll  never forget that day i know you won't  either because i know you were there but  yesterday i was watching you on  television i felt your pain i felt your  passion  it literally jumped through me jumped  out of the tv screen to me chris when  you started begging your colleagues  begging your colleagues so i'm wondering  what has been the reaction have you  heard from them have they said we hear  you we believe you now is the time to do  something what are they saying to you  today  i mean listen i i just worry that we are  becoming numb to this that we are  accepting this as the new normal we just  need to remind ourselves that this is  the only place in the world that this  happens there's not a single country in  the world in which kids fear for their  lives when they walk into school in the  morning it's our choice we can do  something about this and so  yes i've been on the phone texting with  my colleagues all yesterday this morning  trying to find some common ground listen  no secret that i think these assault  weapons designed to kill human beings as  quickly as possible have no place in  civilized society but i'm willing to  compromise and so i've made clear to my  republican colleagues i'm open for  business um if you have a compromise if  you have something that you think can  make our country a little bit safer it  can make our kids and our families a  little bit safer let's get it done and  so my hope is over the next 24-48 hours  that they'll be you know 10 or 15  republicans of good conscience that will  watch what these parents are going  through in texas and come to the table  and try to find some way to make sure  that this doesn't happen at least as  often as it does now as a parent who is  sending his two school-age kids off to  school this morning again  knowing that those kids are talking to  each other today about whether their  school is next week  imagine the conversations that parents  are having with their children this  morning we we were told that you were  talking to senator manchin this morning  can you share where he stands on this  issue  well you know senator manchin was you  know one of the leaders uh after sandy  hook in trying to find bipartisan  compromise on expanding background  checks and so  senator mancha and i were just on the  phone we're going to be reaching out to  republicans today to see if we can find  some of that  common ground whether it's on red flag  laws trying to take guns away from folks  who show significant signs of  impending danger or whether it's a  smaller expansion of the background  check system we're going to reach out to  republicans try to find something that  we can do together this year right now  senator you've talked about common sense  gun legislation what does that actually  look like to you  you know what's wild is that this issue  is only controversial inside washington  dc outside washington dc there's more  consensus on common sense gun  legislation than on almost any other  topic 90 of americans think that every  gun purchase should come with a  background check the majority of  republicans in this country don't think  that assault weapons should be legal so  when i say common sense gun legislation  i mean changes in our gun laws that are  supported by a cross-section of gun  owners and non-gun owners republicans  and democrats in this country  this is an issue that outside of this  place actually has tons of consensus and  you know that's the gap that we're  trying to close here  senator no place is sacred no person is  safe even your colleagues in congress  have been  targeted on a baseball field no less  practicing for a game so at what point  are the people who are  tasked with  giving legislation for a bill that as  you say is bipartisan going to act is it  going to take an act by the president an  executive order of some kind  i think there's only so much that the  president can do on his own  you know a lot of my republican  colleagues still labor under this  mythology that  more guns make us safer well you heard  the reporting just minutes ago from  texas  there were armed police officers outside  that school when the gunman arrived and  they could not stop him in part because  he had weapons that were just as if not  more powerful than  the police had our police are out gunned  today by these shooters and so we've got  to disabuse members of congress of this  idea that the way to protect kids is to  put more weapons in our schools  obviously that didn't work here what we  have to do is make sure that the killers  don't have weapons that are more  powerful than law enforcement  senator i just think we really need a  hero here in the senate we need a hero  in this country you know it's democrats  blame republicans republicans blame  democrats what if the focus was somehow  just focused on the children right i  don't know anybody republican or  democrat if you just say this is about  children because it it keeps happening  over and over and over again and nothing  ever changes  how do we get to people to get to  people's hearts to say what can we do  you know it's more heinous to me that  these were elementary school kids who  were just sitting in their desks with  their baby teeth i cannot stop thinking  about that and i know you know the same  thing about newtown why not just ask  people how do you feel about children we  say we care about children in this  country over guns  that doesn't seem to be the case based  on the actions that have been taken  before  yeah and that's what i said on the floor  yesterday you know why i spent all this  time get coming to congress  running for the united states senate and  then do  nothing do nothing slaughter after  slaughter so i think democrats need to  be very clear that we are not going to  insist on the perfect we are willing to  compromise but i think voters and  parents have to stand up right now and  tell their members of congress in  particular they're republican members of  congress come to the table and support  um compromise and if you don't we're not  interested in you representing us  anymore i think that's what parents all  across the country have to say is that  listen we're not going to send you back  to washington if your answer in the face  of these murders is to sit on your hands  ultimately we've got to be responsible  but voters have got to take  responsibility as well  senator you told us that you just talked  to mention has any other republicans  reached out to you since this has  happened yeah i was in touch yesterday  with some of my republican friends in  particular the two texas uh senators uh  in the past uh senator cornyn of texas  has been um willing to sit down at the  table and talk about potential  compromise i'll spend most of today  trying to see if there's that common  ground maybe we just have to force a  vote maybe we just have to put a bill on  the floor of the senate and and and  force an up or down vote but before we  do that let's take some time to try to  find a way to  maybe engage in some compromise on  background checks on red flag laws on  you know exactly who's able to buy these  assault weapons  senator thank you so much we appreciate  you

